From 144346f9fe3374746597c2c046bf8c6a3135a8e7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 08:30:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Stack instead of waiting: same repo, across layers, and
 bottom-up merges
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Owner ruling, 2026-11-07 (about 08:25Z): "Make sure siblings know they
dont need to wait for a merge to start working on a feature branch
needing a dependent feature branch. They can stack. Update
processes/skills".

- continual-progress §"Stack instead of waiting": same repo (branch from
  the dependency PR's branch, draft PR with that base, merge commits, never
  rebase or force-push another's branch); across layers (overlay the
  dependency's branch; a draft may pin its full head SHA); "stacked on
  <repo>#<n>" in the body; when the base lands, retarget, merge main in,
  re-pin to the merge commit, then mark ready.
- coordinate rule 5: stack rather than wait.
- merge-manager-watcher rule 9: stacks merge bottom-up; a stacked
  folio-assistant PR is train-labelled only after its retarget.
- remote-mount §"Stacking across layers": the draft-only full-SHA pin,
  reconciled with "never pin a branch" and "pins move only forward".
- merge-request.bpmn: "Depends on an unmerged PR?" -> "Stack on it and
  keep working" -> "When the base lands, retarget" -> "Make the PR ready",
  before the merge manager check. SVG, checklist and .pot regenerated;
  bpmn:detangle --check has no finding.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VQDpPc2tT1vUufdyDbQTBz
